DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 5, 2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<5, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<5, 2>") . Compute("<10, 8>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<10, 8>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, -1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -1, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 3, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, -1>") . Compute("<3, -10>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<3, -10>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-1, -10>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-1, -10>") x Compute("<6, -1>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<6, -1>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 6, 1 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 9, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -6, -10 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<9, 8>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, 1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -10>") x Compute("<9, 8>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<6, 1>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -4, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -5>") x Compute("<-4, -10>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -10>") . Compute("<-4, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -10>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 0, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, 7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 7>") x Compute("<0, -8>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<7, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 7>") . Compute("<0, -8>")}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, 7>") x Compute("<0, -9>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -8>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -9 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 6, -3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<6, -3>") x Compute("<-4, -9>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<6, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-4, -9>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
